const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"随机化的是建树过程",en:"Randomize tree construction, then aggregate"},body:{zh:"Breiman把森林定义为一组依赖随机向量的树分类器，每棵树对类别投票。随机化可以来自样本抽取或特征选择；最终输出来自多棵树的组合，而不是挑出训练表现最好的一棵树，也不是随机给出类别。",en:"Breiman defines a forest as tree classifiers built using random vectors, with each tree voting for a class. Randomness may enter sample or feature selection. The output aggregates trees rather than selecting the best training tree or choosing classes at random."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §1.1",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §1.1"}}},{title:{zh:"树强不强与彼此像不像同时重要",en:"Strength and dependence matter together"},body:{zh:"论文用单棵分类器的强度与树之间的相关性解释泛化误差上界。若所有树重复相同错误，增加数量帮助有限；随机选择特征旨在降低依赖，同时保留分类能力。上界是理解机制的工具，并非每个数据集的精确误差公式。",en:"A generalization-error bound combines classifier strength and dependence between trees. Repeating the same errors limits the benefit of more trees. Random feature selection seeks diversity while retaining useful predictions; the bound is not an exact error formula for every dataset."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §2.1–2.2",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §2.1–2.2"}}},{title:{zh:"自助抽样与节点特征抽取分开",en:"Separate bootstrap sampling from node feature selection"},body:{zh:"作者实验中，每棵树的训练样本有放回抽取，同时在节点分裂时随机选择一组输入特征，树不剪枝。这是两种不同的随机化。记录随机种子之外，还需要说明抽样单位、特征数量与建树设置，才能解释复现差异。",en:"The experiments draw each training sample with replacement and randomly select candidate inputs at split nodes, growing unpruned trees. These are distinct sources of randomness. A seed alone is insufficient: record sampling units, feature counts and tree settings."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §3.1; §4",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §3.1; §4"}}},{title:{zh:"袋外预测只使用没见过该行的树",en:"Out-of-bag predictions exclude trees trained on that row"},body:{zh:"一行数据的袋外预测，只聚合训练样本没有包含它的那些树的投票，再与真实标签比较。这不是拿全部树对训练集预测。因为每行的可用树集合不同，也应明确森林规模以及袋外误差的计算方式。",en:"For a row, out-of-bag prediction aggregates only trees whose bootstrap samples excluded it, then compares the result with its label. This differs from applying all trees to the training set. Each row uses a different subset of trees, so the aggregation convention matters."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §3.1",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §3.1"}}},{title:{zh:"打乱变量后变差，不等于因果作用",en:"Permutation importance is not a causal effect"},body:{zh:"原文通过打乱袋外样本某个变量，观察误分类率变化来讨论重要性。相关变量可能携带相似信息，因此单独打乱的重要性与加入变量后的增量价值不同。这个诊断衡量模型依赖，不代表改变现实中的变量会造成对应结果。",en:"The manuscript permutes an input in out-of-bag rows and measures the change in misclassification. Correlated inputs can carry overlapping information, so permutation importance differs from incremental value after another variable is included. Model reliance is not an intervention's causal effect."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §10",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §10"}}},{title:{zh:"袋外不等于时间外",en:"Out-of-bag is not out-of-time"},body:{zh:"编辑应用边界：随机留出的行可能与训练行共享公司、日期或重叠的结果窗口。原文的袋外机制并未自动保证金融研究的时间隔离。用于带时间的数据时，还应保留标签可用日、分组和按先后顺序划分的独立测试。",en:"Editorial application: randomly held-out rows may share firms, dates or overlapping outcome windows with training rows. The paper's out-of-bag mechanism does not automatically provide temporal separation. Time-indexed work also needs label availability, grouping and an independent chronological test."},reference:{url:"https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/users/breiman/randomforest2001.pdf",label:{zh:"2001年1月作者稿 · §2.1; §3.1",en:"January 2001 author manuscript · §2.1; §3.1"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2001年1月作者稿，正式期刊引用不变。树数增加时的收敛并不消除数据泄漏、重复调参或市场变化；算法重要性不是因果解释，本文也不是金融预测效果证明。",en:"The guide uses the January 2001 author manuscript, separately from the journal citation. Convergence as trees increase does not remove leakage, repeated tuning or distribution shifts. Variable importance is not causality, and this is not evidence of financial predictive performance."}};export{e as default};
